ps2sdk libpfs: free every zone of an inode with indirect segments (SEGI)

pfsBitmapFreeInodeBlocks() (iop/hdd/libpfs/src/bitmap.c) frees all zones
of a deleted file or directory.  Two mistakes when the zone list continues
in a SEGI block:

1. `bi` is taken before the switch to the next segment, so at the first
   entry of each SEGI it frees data[0] of the previous descriptor (the
   inode's own zone, or the previous SEGI) a second time instead of the
   SEGI's own zone.
2. The loop bound re-reads number_data through `clink` after it has moved
   to the SEGI.  A SEGI has no number_data field (those bytes are part of
   its data[] array, normally 0), so the loop ends there.

Every SEGI and every extent listed in SEGIs therefore stays marked used in
the bitmap: rm of such a file leaks zones and fsck reports "bitmap
unmatch".  Files with more than 113 extents are affected (fragmented
files; Linux ps2fs creates them as Sony's driver does).  Callers: unlink,
rmdir and rename-over (pfs_fio.c, dir.c) and fssk.

Present in ps2sdk master f1ca58a (2026-11-01) and in the submodule of
pfsshell 52b8e83 (ps2sdk 39a8992); libpfs is unchanged between them.
Whether Sony's own PFS.IRX has the same bug is not known.

Verified with tests/ps2fs-qemu: after phase 2, `rm` of the three
fragmented files fragA/fragB/fragC through pfsshell gives
  unpatched: 3219 zones used, NOT CLEAN (bitmap unmatch)
  patched:   3006 zones used, clean
Apply in a ps2sdk checkout with: git apply ps2sdk-pfs-free-segi.patch

diff --git a/iop/hdd/libpfs/src/bitmap.c b/iop/hdd/libpfs/src/bitmap.c
index 6c829e3..db2ecd0 100644
--- a/iop/hdd/libpfs/src/bitmap.c
+++ b/iop/hdd/libpfs/src/bitmap.c
@@ -366,13 +366,13 @@ void pfsBitmapShow(pfs_mount_t *pfsMount)
 void pfsBitmapFreeInodeBlocks(pfs_cache_t *clink)
 {
 	pfs_mount_t *pfsMount=clink->pfsMount;
-	u32 i;
+	u32 i, number_data=clink->u.inode->number_data;
 
 	pfsCacheUsedAdd(clink);
-	for(i=0;i < clink->u.inode->number_data; i++)
+	for(i=0;i < number_data; i++)
 	{
 		u32 index = pfsFixIndex(i);
-		pfs_blockinfo_t *bi=&clink->u.inode->data[index];
+		pfs_blockinfo_t *bi;
 		int err;
 
 		if(i!=0) {
@@ -381,6 +381,7 @@ void pfsBitmapFreeInodeBlocks(pfs_cache_t *clink)
 					return;
 		}
 
+		bi=&clink->u.inode->data[index];
 		pfsBitmapFreeBlockSegment(pfsMount, bi);
 		pfsCacheMarkClean(pfsMount, (u16)bi->subpart,  bi->number << pfsMount->inode_scale,
 			(bi->number + bi->count) << pfsMount->inode_scale);
